      "problem": "$2a+8(\\frac{5a}{2}-\\frac{b}{4})=${{field-1}}\n$a\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$b$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the distributive law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+8(\\frac{5a}{2}-\\frac{b}{4}) & = \\\\ 2a+8(\\frac{5a}{2})-8(\\frac{b}{4}) & = \\\\ 2a+\\frac{40a}{2}-\\frac{8b}{4} & = \\\\ 2a+20a-2b & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we collect and combine the like terms, simplifying the coefficients as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+20a-2b & = \\\\ (2a+20a)-2b & = \\\\ 22\\,a-2\\,b\\end{aligned}\n$$",
